<http://ontologydesignpatterns.org/template> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                              dcterms:description "Diagram | Intent: | The Template Instance pattern proposes a way of reducing the number of reified instances and the related property assertion axioms in an ontology, especially for the cases in which the reified relations are identical for multiple entities. ..."^^xsd:string ;
                                              dcterms:title "Template Instance Pattern"^^xsd:string ;
                                              rdfs:comment """Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK's quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label added x3; term declared x2;
- header: dcterms:title \"Template Instance Pattern\" - the library's name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library's description of the pattern
Each change is listed under \"curated\" in the pattern's metadata.json in OntoBoard's pattern library."""@en .

